    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0270" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/2957</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2586</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-25">November 25, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State refers to the Embassy’s 5025 of November 4, 1943<anchor
                        n="18" xml:id="d237-f1"/> referring to a credit of $300,000 made available
                    to the Cuban National Development Commission by the Export-Import Bank for the
                    rehabilitation of the telegraph and telephone system of the Cuban
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The credit under reference is included in the Attached list of projects approved
                    by the Export-Import Bank, totaling $23,757,230.78.</p>
                <p>[See the enclosure printed on facing page.]</p>



                <xi:include href="d237-a1.xml" xpointer="d237-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
